+/*
+ * The coexistence environment, brought up the way ESP-IDF brings it up.
+ *
+ * This is not the same thing as the _coex_* stubs above, and the
+ * difference cost a board run to find. Those are the OS interface the
+ * blob calls; this is the blob's own coex layer, which has to be
+ * initialised before esp_wifi_init_internal() registers its scheduler
+ * callbacks. IDF does it from its SECONDARY system-init hook, which is
+ * host-side code this port does not have, so nothing was calling it.
+ *
+ * s31 hit the same wall and says so in firmware/radio/radio_stack.c:
+ * "ESP-IDF normally performs these two calls together from its SECONDARY
+ * system-init hook. Registering the adapter alone leaves the coexistence
+ * lock/environment uninitialised; esp_wifi_init() then faults as soon as
+ * it registers its scheduler callbacks."
+ *
+ * esp_coex_adapter_register() and coex_pre_init() are both exported by
+ * libcoexist.a, so they are reachable from here without linking anything
+ * new. If either is missing at link time the build says so, which is the
+ * right failure: a silent skip here is a fault inside the blob later.
+ */
+extern int esp_coex_adapter_register(const void *funcs);
+extern int coex_pre_init(void);
